ider something like: ``` static constexpr auto kEnvToChannel = base::MakeFixedFlatMap<std::string_view, version_info::Channel>( {{\"beta\", version_info::Channel::BETA}, {\"canary\",…"],["42bed852_51b855b4",111,-2,1,"Not going to work for someone building with *BSD and other Unices?"],["567ce961_9101b2b0",112,-2,1,"Should this be NOTREACHED()?"],["5a4aed69_690aeeb6",110,-2,1,"nit: remove `const` from this member and `std::move(...)` here to avoid a copy"],["6179f17d_c832ab75",113,-2,1,"could this live in //base/test with other test support stuff?"],["6add4e77_66fd1540",109,-2,1,"`std::string()` rather than `\"\"` to construct an empty string"],["70c51c24_ead19aa8",110,-2,1,"nit: `{}` or `std::string()`"],["77555af1_819d7eeb",109,-2,1,"consider `static constexpr std::string_view kAppName = ...` as per https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/chromium-dev/c/OXxJy5L96jI/m/tRZHIeZwAgAJ."],["802eab22_e5666781",110,-2,1,"consider `CHECK_EQ(channel, version_info::Channel::STABLE)` here"],["aadaf7fc_eba2a0b6",109,-2,1,"nit: use `base::StrCat({...});` rather than `+=` to combine strings."],["c9449cb1_61bccf4a",114,-2,1,"It's not obvious that this file is 'nix-only. Consider renaming it? In addition, maybe include build/build_config.h here, and then add: `static_assert(BUILDFLAG(IS_POSIX) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC));`…"],["ce03d9c1_026c68be",115,-2,0,"maybe it's 17 years too late for this, but should the environment variable have a different name for non-Google Chrome builds?"],["f58964b6_573dbcc3",116,-2,1,"Are the code in the if/else section the same, except for chrome vs. chromium? Maybe just conditionally define the expectation strings instead?"],["f7b5a8fc_f1f3a9c0",110,-2,1,"replace this with `case version_info::UNKNOWN` so that we get a compile error here if anyone ever adds a new enumerator -- we'll most likely need to adjust the logic here in that case."],["fde72fdd_2fe6fa20",115,-2,1,"this file does more than just channel-related stuff. is `channel.h` really the best name? if everything here is specific to `CHROME_VERSION_EXTRA` (which i confess to not liking in //base -- it's a…"],["1cba5b13_cb1fe139",117,-1,1,"apologies for not mentioning this in the first round: pass by non-const ref rather than by pointer since this is a non-optional input as per…"],["b58af7cd_995c59c5",83,-1,1,"very optional nit: if `env` is not used after this point, could inline `base::Environment::Create()` here."],["3fdd04f9_e0d41879",118,0,0,"Huh, I didn't realize //base/nix files are set up this way. I'm surprised nobody adjusted this."]],0,2257],[7172364,20412,594,9.607,7.821,[[110,0.488,1,294],[111,0.181,1,108],[101,0.092,13,54],[83,0.081,30,48],[53,0.074,14,43],[54,0.051,20,30],[112,0.013,29,7],[113,0.013,15,7],[114,0.007,18,3]],[],0,2258],[7180263,20412,233,3.856,3.092,[[11,144]],[["c75958dd_4b4d7722",119,0,0,"(Just kidding) In the spirit of i18n, this should be \"f6n\"."]],0,2259],[7180182,20413,36,1.22,0.938,[[11,145]],[["67cf1c25_a54fe5e5",1,-1,1,"\"is to call gsk_render_node_draw()\""],["8f6b1e79_4c472a52",120,-1,0,"Separately, is this still necessary, or will CairoSurface overwrite the `pixels` content anyway?"],["b693cf14_bfd19ef4",120,-1,1,"Does this still need to be `SkColor*`, if the SkColorSetA() call that interacted with it is gone?"]],0,2260],[7186409,20413,78,2.717,2.101,[[115,0.511,128,43],[8,0.267,43,19],[11,0.111,146,8],[116,0.111,68,8]],[["9f5a31bb_b7e4de97",14,0,1,"Leave this in? Same in other files."],["dc5203b1_b8b8b2a7",121,0,1,"Was better without this blank line?"]],0,2261],[7157476,20418,514,9.607,7.821,[[53,15]],[["06a22a56_b79bc907",122,-5,1,"these are duplicate definitions; can we pull them out into some shared .h file?"],["01ffca99_4c7e622a",123,-1,1,"Not used."],["155cda25_fd671fff",122,-1,1,"const"],["3319888d_0208778f",124,-1,1,"<map>"],["5e6ef6bd_db438811",124,-1,1,"Probably should do this at the top of the function. Otherwise `state_` access may have been racy."],["6fdf636b_4082b34a",1,-1,1,"No need for a bullet point when there's only 1 item."],["7f8503af_bf4d2b1d",124,-1,1,"Cam also CHECK_EQ() `state_` is transitioning from kIdle to kInitializing."],["d6bb94c2_5daa2f08",125,-1,1,"Add `inline` to all these."]],0,2261],[7204667,20418,62,1.341,1.058,[[12,388]],[["6e6569e8_b2abbbe9",104,-1,0,"Do you know why the existing code doesn't check the status?"]],0,2262],[7205152,20418,890,9.607,7.821,[[40,1.0,150,914]],[["d14ae224_4831d73f",1,0,0,"In my mind, I thought someone would have added a //.style.yapf to default to, but nope, not in Chromium."]],0,2263],[7201054,20418,1870,8.912,7.201,[[40,0.833,151,2334],[117,0.167,2,468]],[["0605ba59_a33078af",1,-1,1,"Should also mention why do the switch."],["0acf63c8_7f9e0116",126,-1,0,"This feels like a very literal translation from the Bash script. Can the Installer class put the original package name somewhere else other than in its context? Maybe as a follow-up?"],["0eb44af1_d52ef230",127,-1,1,"Var only used once. Combine."],["18c64cdc_d2284918",126,-1,1,"Also sort these 3."],["1b8dca80_ae88f9fa",126,-1,1,"`\"..\", \"common\"`"],["2138ad9c_c5b8666b",127,-1,1,"Can the if and else blocks share the path and only differ by the file name?"],["265cefd5_a35694d5",127,-1,1,"Save the path to a variable and reuse."],["2c24e748_48dd1731",126,-1,1,"do_package() doesn't exist anymore? i.e. Comment won't make sense in the future."],["7810d4d8_ac1da4bb",127,-1,1,"Are src and dest already Path objects when passed in?"],["79c7a950_f4f742ac",127,-1,1,"Another example of something that feels too literally translated. The class can just store this in a separate field."],["94c31135_c08c6f15",127,-1,1,"Sort. Consider auto-formatting all the new Python files."],["a4d5ff19_290c6bc0",128,-1,1,"Can this be a relative path?"],["a50afcc7_d7f91623",127,-1,1,"Cam just be a == comparison, like line 78."],["b00fa301_be9625e2",127,-1,1,"Can the permissions be stored as an int in its own member variable? Then no need to do string to int conversions."],["b68d143f_1489d26d",126,-1,1,"Can the script omit line 89 and use args.channel where needed, so the variable doesn't get reassigned here? Then the same variable doesn't take on 2 different meanings."],["cb2a0bc5_5dfeee76",127,-1,1,"Unused, replace with underscore?"],["cb33fa4b_f8c3ee0d",129,-1,1,"Comment seems unnecessary, given most other chmod calls don't have comments."],["db714d9f_80071448",130,-1,1,"Can this be at the end, near line 169, instead of being at the beginning?"],["e1d7105b_f43b5ac9",126,-1,1,"If it doesn't matter, just sort by the key?"],["fbb4ec18_e121f505",127,-1,1,"It may be better if there was a separate method that handled this case and then called _install() with the updated destination. Then it is clearer from looking at the calls to see what will happen."]],0,2264],[7204746,20418,83,2.212,1.739,[[56,0.931,35,78],[71,0.069,6,5]],[["daeabc2b_99967998",131,-1,0,"Would it make sense to do this at line 291 and not depend on any particular test expectation config?"]],0,2265],[7204763,20418,75,1.661,1.339,[[54,21]],[["c9deaf06_e2636ab1",50,-1,0,"BTW, I think this can be simplified given line 135."]],0,2266],[7204285,20418,19,0.67,0.502,[[55,27]],[],0,2267],[7204965,20418,160,3.856,3.092,[[53,16]],[["8af58303_cd5ec555",132,-1,1,"Simplify to `using SetSystemdScopeUnitNameForXdgPortalTest = ::testing::Test;`"],["8fcb0103_855d61ee",133,-1,1,"WDYT about moving to namespace dbus_xdg::internal?"],["ab423c24_237e3acb",83,-1,1,"No longer used."],["cfefe459_fd415a46",83,-1,1,"Does it still make sense to have this boolean, if the class can also check if `callbacK_` is null or not?"],["54d91f50_a301f7e8",133,0,1,"No longer used."],["6eec0e51_fd1b1231",83,0,1,"No longer used."]],0,2268],[7214586,20430,414,6.547,5.298,[[55,0.582,28,246],[53,0.32,17,134],[8,0.037,43,15],[12,0.019,389,6],[56,0.019,36,6],[54,0.019,22,6],[11,0.005,146,1]],[["04dd17ed_e8b21f47",1,-5,1,"Wrap at 72 columns."],["4b7fb4b1_6f3f3118",1,-5,1,"\"In SelectFileDialogLinuxPortal, owning_window ...\" for context."